            {
              "id": "b306b931-7bde-3ef4-8c33-14b9afe63cfc",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the classification indicates a risk of undefined behavior due to the possibility that either the destination or source pointer may be null. The verdict for this call site is also marked as 'GENUINE', confirming the high confidence in this assessment. The code copies a string literal into a destination buffer using a function that does not guarantee null-termination if the buffer size is reached, and there is no explicit check to ensure that the destination pointer is not null before the operation. The source is a string literal, which is always valid, but the destination pointer could be null, as there is no guard or validation present. This could lead to a crash or other undefined behavior if the function is called with a null destination pointer.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore copying the string, ensure that the destination pointer is not null. This prevents undefined behavior if the pointer is invalid. Also, after using `strncpy`, explicitly null-terminate the destination buffer to avoid unterminated strings if the source is longer than the buffer size.\n\n```c\nif (status && status->vbios_version) {\n    strncpy(status->vbios_version, \"022.040.003.041.000001\", AGA_MAX_STR_LEN);\n    status->vbios_version[AGA_MAX_STR_LEN - 1] = '\\0';\n}\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n\n___\n"
