              "id": "ec2e17f4-c403-3082-be15-2c709d2f7587",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the classification indicates a risk of undefined behavior due to the possibility that either the source or destination pointer may be null. The code copies a string literal into a destination buffer using a function that does not check if the destination pointer is valid. There is no evidence of a guard or check to ensure the destination pointer is not null before the operation. The source is a string literal, which is always valid, but the destination may be null, as indicated by the analysis. This can lead to a crash or other undefined behavior if the destination pointer is not properly initialized. The absence of a null-termination guarantee after the copy further increases the risk. Developers should ensure that all pointers are valid before performing such operations and consider adding explicit null checks.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore copying the string literal into the destination buffer, ensure that the destination pointer is not null. Add an explicit check to prevent undefined behavior:\n\n```c\nif (status && status->driver_version) {\n    strncpy(status->driver_version, \"6.3.6\", AGA_MAX_STR_LEN);\n    status->driver_version[AGA_MAX_STR_LEN - 1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\n}\n```\nThis approach prevents dereferencing a null pointer and ensures the destination buffer is always null-terminated, which is important when using `strncpy`.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n___\n"
