            {
              "id": "65afbd2f-129c-393c-a5a1-afd82301de98",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is considered a genuine vulnerability because the code copies a string into a destination buffer using a function that does not guarantee null-termination, and there are no visible checks to ensure that the destination pointer is not null before the operation. The source is a C-style string, which is generally safe, but the destination pointer may be null, as there is no evidence of a guard or validation before use. This can lead to undefined behavior if the destination is null. Additionally, there is no explicit null-termination after the copy, which can also cause issues if the source string is longer than the maximum allowed length. The classification specifically highlights the risk of null pointer dereference, and the verdict confirms this is a genuine issue.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nBefore copying the string, ensure that the destination pointer (`fw_version` and `fw_version->firmware`) is not null. Also, after using `strncpy`, explicitly null-terminate the destination buffer to prevent unterminated strings if the source is too long. For example:\n\n```cpp\nif (fw_version && fw_version->firmware) {\n    strncpy(fw_version->firmware, block_name.c_str(), AGA_MAX_STR_LEN);\n    fw_version->firmware[AGA_MAX_STR_LEN - 1] = '\\0';\n}\n```\nThis ensures that the destination is valid and always null-terminated, preventing undefined behavior and potential security issues.\n\n## References\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/476.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS111237"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "b57e4f75-1e44-35a1-b675-af467c4557f2",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis detected a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the memory copy operation. The dataflow analysis indicates that the destination and source may refer to overlapping memory, which is not allowed for memcpy and can result in unpredictable program behavior. Additionally, there is no evidence that the destination pointer is always valid (it may be null), further increasing the risk. The use of a minimum function to limit the copy length does not mitigate the undefined behavior risk if the regions overlap. There are no explicit guards or null-termination after the copy, and the destination's capacity is not clearly defined. All these factors confirm the issue is genuine and not a false positive.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory where the source and destination regions may overlap, use `memmove` instead of `memcpy`. `memmove` is designed to handle overlapping memory safely. Replace the original call with:\n\n```cpp\nmemmove(api_spec->id, proto_key.data(), SDK_MIN(proto_key.length(), OBJ_MAX_KEY_LEN));\n```\n\nAdditionally, ensure that `api_spec->id` is a valid, non-null pointer before the call to avoid null pointer dereference. If possible, add a check:\n\n```cpp\nif (api_spec && api_spec->id) {\n    memmove(api_spec->id, proto_key.data(), SDK_MIN(proto_key.length(), OBJ_MAX_KEY_LEN));\n}\n```\n\n## References\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS121708"
                ]
              }
