            {
              "id": "777b308f-12d1-3226-8ac4-db9e906623c1",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the strncpy operation. The dataflow analysis suggests that the destination buffer and the source expression may refer to overlapping memory, which is not allowed by the strncpy function and can result in unpredictable program behavior. Additionally, the source may be null at this call site, which further increases the risk of undefined behavior. There is no explicit null-termination of the destination buffer after the copy, and no guard is present to ensure safe operation. The destination is not a pointer-based member, which slightly reduces the risk of null pointer dereference, but the overlap and null source risks remain significant. These factors indicate a high-confidence, actionable issue that should be addressed to prevent potential security and stability problems.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo remediate the undefined behavior risk caused by possible overlapping memory regions in the strncpy operation, ensure that the source and destination buffers do not overlap. If there is any chance of overlap, use a memory-safe function such as memmove, which is designed to handle overlapping regions safely. Additionally, always check that the source is not null before performing the copy, and explicitly null-terminate the destination buffer after the copy to prevent unterminated strings.\n\nExample fix:\n\n```cpp\nif (event_description_(args->events[e]) != nullptr) {\n    // Use memmove if overlap is possible\n    memmove(event_data[num_elem].message, event_description_(args->events[e]), MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE);\n    // Ensure null-termination\n    event_data[num_elem].message[MAX_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_MSG_SIZE - 1] = '\\0';\n}\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
