            {
              "id": "87d79ada-a631-372b-a642-6752f0bbde67",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Production Code Debugging Vulnerability\" in C++ is a type of software vulnerability that occurs when debugging code is inadvertently left in the production code. This can lead to a variety of security risks, including information disclosure, unauthorized access, and even remote code execution. In the provided code snippet, there doesn't seem to be a direct debugging vulnerability. However, if the port number (`AGA_DEFAULT_RDC_GRPC_SERVER_PORT`) is not properly validated or secured, it could potentially be exploited.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this type of vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n- Always remove debugging code or statements before deploying the application to production.\n- Use preprocessor directives or build flags to ensure debugging code is not included in the production build.\n- Regularly use static code analysis tools to detect potential vulnerabilities in the code.\n- Validate and sanitize all inputs, including port numbers, to prevent potential attacks.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn the provided code snippet, ensure that the port number is validated and sanitized. For example:\n\n```cpp\n#include <stdexcept>\n\n#define MIN_PORT 0\n#define MAX_PORT 65535\n\nint validatePort(int port) {\n    if (port < MIN_PORT || port > MAX_PORT) {\n        throw std::invalid_argument(\"Invalid port number\");\n    }\n    return port;\n}\n\n// ...\n\nstd::string serverAddress = \"127.0.0.1:\" + std::to_string(validatePort(AGA_DEFAULT_RDC_GRPC_SERVER_PORT));\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet requires the following libraries:\n\n- `<stdexcept>` for handling exceptions.\n- `<string>` for string manipulation.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Code Review Guide](https://owasp.org/www-project-code-review-guide/)\n- [CWE-489: Active Debug Code](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/489.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS162092"
                ]
              }
